# Fur Elise, the opening section (repertoire plan: fur-elise-theme). Beethoven's A section as a
# single line, an octave below the piano's right hand, with its repeat (first ending back to the
# start, second ending on the final A). The rocking E D# E D# E B D C A sits on the open string 1
# (E), string 2 fret 4 (D#, finger 4), string 2 fret 3 (D, finger 3), string 2 fret 1 (C, finger 1),
# the open string 2 (B) and string 3 fret 2 (A, finger 2). Each answer climbs a chord from the bass
# strings: C E A (Am) and E G# B (E), with G# on string 3 fret 1, never the open G.
# The piano's left-hand notes are left out (they lie below the guitar's range an octave down).
# The notes are the A section as it is commonly printed (the common editions all descend from
# the 1867 first edition). They have not yet been checked against a scan of that edition, which
# the repertoire plan asks for.
title: Für Elise (theme)
id: fur-elise-theme
composer: Ludwig van Beethoven
source: Bagatelle in A minor, WoO 59 (composed 1810, first published 1867); A section arranged as a single line for Sixstring Academy
arranger: Sixstring Academy
licence: Public domain (Beethoven died in 1827); this arrangement is original to Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 4
tags: melody, classical, 3/8, minor key, sixteenth notes
tempo: 60
time: 3/8
key: Am
pickup: e

track: Melody
role: lead
